{"availability":"available","full":"Srivatsa03/rag-redteam","name":"rag-redteam","description":"Red-team your RAG pipeline for prompt injection, source-document leakage, and cross-document smuggling, in CI. The gap between RAG eval (RAGAS/DeepEval) and LLM scanners (garak).","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","stars":28,"forks":4,"created":"2026-06-26T03:31:50Z","updated":"2026-10-15T01:10:36Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://pypi.org/project/rag-redteam/","topics":["ai-security","devsecops","github-actions","llm-security","prompt-injection","python","rag","red-teaming"],"demo":"https://srivatsa03.github.io/rag-redteam/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T11:30:02.848Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T11:30:02.848Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T11:30:02.848Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:49.729Z","stars":29,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-12T06:28:04.135Z","stars":29,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-18T11:30:02.848Z","stars":28,"forks":4}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Red-team your RAG pipeline for prompt injection and source-document leakage, right in CI.","RAG systems have an attack surface that general LLM scanners miss: the retrieved documents themselves. An attacker who can get text into your knowledge base can plant instructions the model will later obey (indirect prompt injection), or coax the system into spilling its private sources (data leakage). rag-redteam attacks your pipeline the way an adversary would and fails your build if it's exploitable.","It's deliberately the gap between two existing tools:"],"features":["RAG eval frameworks (RAGAS, DeepEval) measure answer quality, not security.","LLM scanners (garak, LLM Guard) probe the model, not your retrieval pipeline."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Srivatsa03/rag-redteam/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"7cb69d0bfc609e73b2cd6595cea20ee2b7d2fa1f74ab1b9374d2f1b824380419","extractedAt":"2